<% content_for :title, "Law Enforcement" %>
<article class="col-lg-9 mx-auto">
  <p class="kicker">Your rights</p>
  <h1>Law enforcement in Malaysia</h1>
  <p class="lead">Several laws protect survivors. Here is a plain-language overview.</p>

  <h2>Domestic Violence Act 1994 (Act 521)</h2>
  <p>The main law covering abuse between spouses, former spouses, children, incapacitated adults and other family members. It was amended in 2012 and 2017, and it recognises emotional and psychological abuse as well as physical harm.</p>
  <ul class="list-group list-group-flush mb-4">
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent"><strong>Protection Order (PO):</strong> issued by a court to stop the abuser from further violence.</li>
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent"><strong>Interim Protection Order (IPO):</strong> a short-term order while the case is pending.</li>
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent"><strong>Emergency Protection Order (EPO):</strong> can be issued quickly through a Social Welfare Officer when there is an urgent risk.</li>
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent">Breaching an order is a criminal offence and can be reported to the police.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Other relevant laws</h2>
  <div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 g-4">
    <%= info_card "Penal Code" do %><p class="text-muted mb-0">Offences such as causing hurt, criminal intimidation, outrage of modesty and rape.</p><% end %>
    <%= info_card "Anti-Sexual Harassment Act 2022" do %><p class="text-muted mb-0">Act 840. Provides a Tribunal for complaints of sexual harassment.</p><% end %>
    <%= info_card "Child Act 2001" do %><p class="text-muted mb-0">Protects children from abuse and neglect.</p><% end %>
    <%= info_card "Islamic family law" do %><p class="text-muted mb-0">Syariah law applies to Muslims for marriage, divorce and maintenance, alongside the civil laws above.</p><% end %>
  </div>

  <h2>How to report</h2>
  <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered mb-4">
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent">Go to the nearest police station or call 999 if in danger. You can lodge a report at any station.</li>
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent">Ask for medical care. Government hospitals have a One Stop Crisis Centre (OSCC).</li>
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent">Keep evidence where it is safe: photos, messages, medical records.</li>
    <li class="list-group-item bg-transparent">Ask the police or Social Welfare Department about a Protection Order.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="alert alert-sage">Legal aid is available through the Legal Aid Department (Jabatan Bantuan Guaman) and several NGOs.</div>
</article>
